---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Routes from "../../components/Routes.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";
import Sequence from "../../components/Sequence.astro";

const ST = "server/src/iki_server/storage";
const SVC = `${ST}/services.py`;
const INV = "plugins/inventory/types";

const H = {
  short: "Where a record is, and every move it made",
  how: "Containers, places, the location ledger and custody",
  example: "A rack moved to another shelf before a defrost",
  rules: "Grids, the ledger and moves as reviewed",
  ref: "Routes, code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "declaring", label: "Declaring containers" },
  { id: "place", label: "A place and the location ledger" },
  { id: "custody", label: "Custody" },
  { id: "move-seq", label: "A bulk move, previewed then committed" },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A type with <code>storage:</code> is kept somewhere, or keeps other records. Each record kept
      somewhere has one place row: a container and position, or a person who has it. Every change is
      an event in an append-only location ledger, audited and sent to webhooks. A move of many records
      is one operation, all or none, and the app commits it only as its preview showed it (<Adr
        n={[180, 207]}
      />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <h3 id="declaring">Declaring containers</h3>
    <p>
      <code>storage:</code> names the types a record holds, its grid, the field holding the code
      already on it, a label line, and which operations need a scan first (<Path
        p="spec/src/iki_spec/model.py"
        sym="class Storage:"
      />). In <code>iki/inventory</code> a freezer holds shelves, a shelf holds racks and boxes, a rack
      is a 5 × 4 grid of boxes, and a box takes its grid from its own fields, fixed when it's made:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file={`${INV}/box.yaml`} start="^storage:" />
    <p>
      A grid's positions are lettered and numbered (A1 to H12) or numbered (1 to 96), along rows or
      down columns, which is also the order they fill in (<Path p={`${ST}/grids.py`} />). A container's
      shape is kept, append-only, the first time it holds something, and the database checks every
      position against it (<Path p={SVC} sym="def ensure_container(" />, <Path
        p={`${ST}/models.py`}
        sym="class Container("
      />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="place">A place and the location ledger</h3>
    <p>
      A record's place is one row: its container, row and column, or its custodian and since when.
      One record per position is a deferred unique constraint, so a swap commits as one change; a
      trigger checks each position against the container's grid; and nothing is in itself (<Path
        p={`${ST}/models.py`}
        sym="class Place("
      />, <Path p={`${ST}/migrations/0001_initial.py`} sym="iki_storage_place_in_grid()" />).
    </p>
    <p>
      Every placement, move, removal, check-out, check-in, hand-over and receipt is an event with
      where from and where to, the custodian, the scan that confirmed it, the operation it belongs to,
      who did it and why. Each is audited as <code>storage.moved</code> and sent to webhooks (<Path
        p={`${ST}/models.py`}
        sym="class Event("
      />, <Path p={SVC} sym="def record_event(" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="custody">Custody</h3>
    <p>
      Checking a record out gives it to a person and keeps its position, which nothing else can take,
      until it's checked in, to that position or another in the same change. A record with someone can
      be handed over to another person, by its custodian or by an Editor of its container's project.
      Putting things in a container, or taking them out, needs Editor in the container's project: it's
      that project's freezer (<Path p={SVC} sym="def check_out(" />, <Path p={SVC} sym="def hand_over(" />, <Path
        p={SVC}
        sym="def keeps("
      />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="move-seq">A bulk move, previewed then committed</h3>
    <Sequence
      id="move-dg"
      title="Moving a rack to another shelf before a defrost"
      width={900}
      actors={[
        { id: "person", label: "Lab member" },
        { id: "app", label: "Web app", sub: "MoveDialog" },
        { id: "api", label: "API", sub: "/storage/moves" },
        { id: "svc", label: "storage.services" },
        { id: "db", label: "Postgres" },
      ]}
      steps={[
        { id: "pick", from: "person", to: "app", label: "records, a destination scan, a reason" },
        { id: "preview", from: "app", to: "api", label: "POST, preview: true" },
        { id: "plan", from: "api", to: "svc", label: "plan(): positions and problems, no locks" },
        { id: "review", from: "app", to: "person", label: "each move and problem, for review", dashed: true },
        { id: "commit", from: "app", to: "api", label: "the same items and the plan, preview: false" },
        { id: "lock", from: "svc", to: "db", label: "lock records and containers, in id order" },
        { id: "replan", from: "svc", to: "svc", label: "plan() again; not the plan shown: 409" },
        { id: "apply", from: "svc", to: "db", label: "places and events, one operation; clash check" },
      ]}
    >
      <div slot="pick"><p>The destination is resolved from its scan. Types that need a scan to move also ask for the records' own scans.</p><p><Path p="web/app/src/storage-ui.tsx" sym="export function MoveDialog(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="preview"><p>The request body names each record and where it goes, with or without a position.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/storage.py" sym="class MovesIn(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="plan"><p>When no position is given, the planner takes the next free one in the container's order.</p><p><Path p={SVC} sym="def plan(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="review"><p>Nothing has changed yet. The preview also returns <code>plan</code>: a SHA-256 of each record, where it is, and the container and position it goes to.</p><p><Path p={SVC} sym="def identify(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="commit"><p>The dialog sends back the plan it showed. An API caller may leave it out; then a position left empty is the next free one when the moves are made.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/storage.py" sym="plan: str | None = Field(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="lock"><p>A record whose location changed since it was read is refused.</p><p><Path p={SVC} sym="def move(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="replan"><p>The plan is computed again under the locks. If it isn't the plan shown, because another placement took a position or a record moved meanwhile, nothing moves: 409 <code>moves_plan_changed</code> carries what the moves would do now, and the dialog shows what changed per record for a fresh confirmation. Otherwise a single problem refuses every move with 422 (<Adr n="0207" />).</p><p><Path p={SVC} sym="raise PlanChanged(planned)" />, <Path p="web/app/src/storage-ui.tsx" sym='"moves_plan_changed"' /></p></div>
      <div slot="apply"><p>The deferred position constraint is checked before commit, so a clash refuses the whole move.</p><p><Path p={SVC} sym="def _check_now(" /></p></div>
    </Sequence>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      Before a freezer is defrosted, a lab member moves a rack of boxes to a shelf in another freezer,
      with the reason "Freezer 2 defrost". A shelf has no grid, so the planner allocates no position;
      the rack's place changes, one <code>moved</code> event is written, and every box in the rack,
      and every tube in each box, keeps its place, since those are places in the rack and the box.
      Where a record is now is read up its chain of containers, at most 16 deep (<Path
        p={SVC}
        sym="def chain("
      />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Bulk moves, as reviewed" open>
        <p>
          Up to 1,536 moves, with one reason, all or none, under one operation. A preview names what it
          shows; confirming sends that name back, and the server compares it with the plan it computes
          under the moves' locks. A different well, source, container or order gives a different name.
          Problems and proofs aren't part of it, since they're checked again when the moves are made
          (<Adr n={[180, 207]} />, <Path p={SVC} sym="MAX_MOVES = 1536" />).
        </p>
        <Excerpt file={SVC} start="^def identify\(" />
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Grids and the location ledger">
        <p>
          A grid is at most 32 by 48, a 1536-well plate's (<Path
            p="spec/src/iki_spec/model.py"
            sym="GRID_POSITIONS = 1536"
          />, <Path p={`${ST}/models.py`} sym='name="iki_storage_container_grid"' />). The kinds of
          event:
        </p>
        <Excerpt file={`${ST}/models.py`} start="^class EventKind\(" />
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Where the ADRs and the code differ">
        <ul>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0139" /> still says where something is kept stays a field and containers aren't
            modelled; <Adr n="0180" /> changed that, and its update note points to <code
              >iki/inventory</code
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0180" />'s example has one declaration for a freezer or a shelf, holding racks and
            boxes. In <code>iki/inventory</code> a freezer holds only shelves, and a shelf holds racks
            and boxes.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <Routes
      tags={["storage"]}
      paths={/^\/api\/v1\/(storage\/(moves|places|check-in|check-out|checked-out|hand-over|scan|labels|containers\/\{ref\}$)|entities\/\{ref\}\/location)/}
    />
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={SVC} />: places, events, custody and moves</li>
        <li><Path p={`${ST}/scan_identity.py`} />, <Path p={`${ST}/labels.py`} />: scanning codes and printing labels</li>
        <li><Path p={INV} />: Freezer, Shelf, Rack, Box and Tube</li>
        <li><Path p="web/app/src/storage-ui.tsx" />: the app's storage dialogs</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0180" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0207" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0211" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
